Published HTTP security backports for PHP 8.0.30.

CVE-2025-1217: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/d20b4c97a9f883b62b65b82d939c5af9a2028ef1
Prerequisites where absent: 1c157d3fa2e102ccf375ec4c1ddca8770208dae7,
51e2015af3fc4757a666736aae7899a43f76ae6d (HTTP chunked redirects and long headers).
CVE-2025-1734: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/0548c4c1756724a89ef8310709419b08aadb2b3b
CVE-2025-1861: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/ac1a054bb3eb5994a199e8b18cca28cbabf5943e
Empty/single-character Location followups: 547566f17a12b4900efb69a7cf8cd325d00613a2,
64664758cd8ee5928acf25b3f9ae11c7571c1b39 (CVE-2026-93682 regression protection).
Test helpers: 95f2583743bdd758d8dbdc7e23e08a4a2d39e8da,
b8731767d83acf5ae2be6a26eab7f6721c94eb64.
Source: Freexian php7.3_7.3.31-1~deb10u16.debian.tar.xz,
SHA256: 1eedbd1095e7be93d310c2cbfd13acbcf521b2433ef0ddb5e40abd2dffa633bb.

Adaptations: retain native URL representation and response-header ownership,
retain existing cross-origin credential stripping, and free the new dynamic
redirect path on native error/recursive-call exits. PHP 7.1/7.2 use their
native zend_string_free API. Native tests retain branch-specific diagnostics.
PHP 7.1/7.2 HTTP test helper binds IPv4 loopback because their socket-name
format does not bracket IPv6 literals. The OpenSSL test helper and HTTP
advisory fixtures already use IPv4 loopback.

